===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Damaged and shabby as a result of much use.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1857|author=w:Herman Melville|title={{w|The Confidence-Man|The Confidence-Man: His Masquerade}}|chapter=XVIII|passage=Upon this, an unhappy-looking woman, in a sort of mourning, neat, but sadly '''worn''', hid her face behind a meagre bundle, and was heard to sob.}}
# {{cap|worn out}}; exhausted.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1889|title=The Wesley Naturalist|volume=2|page=143
|passage=Preëminently is the Lake District suited for the jaded and '''worn''', who seek in solitude and amidst scenery unmoiled and unsullied by human artifice, refreshment alike of body and spirit.}}

